{
 "id": "segment_stiffness.tencer1982.lumbar_joint_preload_displacement_ratio_Rc",
 "title": "Lumbar intervertebral joint: effect of a preload in one direction on flexibility in another (displacement ratio Rc), intact and facets removed",
 "layer": "property",
 "category": "segment_stiffness",
 "subcategory": "preload_effect",
 "region": "lumbar",
 "levels": [
  "L2-L3",
  "L4-L5"
 ],
 "condition": "intact (5 specimens); some load pairs repeated with both facets removed",
 "quantity": {
  "name": "displacement ratio Rc (combined / single loading)",
  "definition": "Rc = mean over increments of (incremental displacement in the variable-load direction WITH a constant preload in another direction) / (same without preload); preload magnitude = max load of Table 3. Values outside 0.90-1.12 were considered significant (circled; 'significant' flag here derived from that rule). Load/displacement coordinate system with origin O_L at the intersection of the disc mid-transverse plane and the line joining the two vertebral body centres (NOT the vertebral body centre); Z along that centre line (axial compression +Fz), Y in the plane of symmetry (antero-posterior, +Fy anterior shear), X lateral (+Fx right lateral shear); rotations G (flexion-extension about X), B (lateral bending about Y; CCW = -B), A (axial rotation about Z; CW = +A). Lower member fixed, upper member unconstrained (loads by pulleys/dead weights).",
  "unit": "ratio"
 },
 "source": {
  "short": "Tencer 1982",
  "authors": "Tencer AF, Ahmed AM, Burke DL",
  "year": 1982,
  "journal": "J Biomech Eng 104:193-201",
  "doi": "10.1115/1.3138348",
  "n": 5,
  "sample": "5 lumbar joints for combined loading (Table 2 tests 2-9 used 4-6 specimens; text: Rc from five specimens); facet-removed subset not specified; human cadaveric lumbar joints, disc grade 1-2, radiographically normal except one hypoplastic L5",
  "age": "16-57 y (57, 18, 33, 16, 53, 57, 37, 48)",
  "sex": "7 M, 1 F (donors)",
  "height_cm": null,
  "weight_kg": null
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Preload equal to the max load of Table 3 applied first, then a variable load in another principal direction in 3 steps to its max. 46 load pairs. Some pairs repeated after removal of both facets. Nucleus pressurised to 626 kPa by water injection before testing (simulating reclining in vivo pressure); 4 conditioning cycles of +-axial torsion at max torque.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model L2-L3/L4-L5 with output at the disc centre O_L; fix lower vertebra",
   "Apply the preload (90 N shear, 823 N compression, 11.2 Nm flexion/extension, 14.7 Nm lateral bending or 12.9 Nm axial torque) and hold it",
   "Apply the variable load in 3 steps to its Table 3 maximum and compute the mean incremental displacement/load ratio; divide by the same ratio without preload",
   "Repeat with both facets removed for the pairs given and compare Rc (ratio < 1 = stiffening)"
  ],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": "Coordinate system: Load/displacement coordinate system with origin O_L at the intersection of the disc mid-transverse plane and the line joining the two vertebral body centres (NOT the vertebral body centre); Z along that centre line (axial compression +Fz), Y in the plane of symmetry (antero-posterior, +Fy anterior shear), X lateral (+Fx right lateral shear); rotations G (flexion-extension about X), B (lateral bending about Y; CCW = -B), A (axial rotation about Z; CW = +A). Lower member fixed, upper member unconstrained (loads by pulleys/dead weights). Text cross-checks: Fz preload reduces axial torque flexibility ~50% (Rc .48), anterior shear by 61% (.39) and posterior shear by 67% (.33)."
 },
